From: claude <claude@deeveeyant.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 01:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] tagger: word-boundary topic matching, drop frequency-word
 and type tags

Auto-generated tags were nonsense on real memories. Three separate causes,
each verified against stored content:

* Topic keywords were matched as bare substrings, so "strips" matched "trip"
  (travel), "rework" matched "work", "restore" matched "store" (shopping).
  Infrastructure notes came back tagged travel and shopping. Now matched on
  word boundaries.
* The three most frequent long words were added as tags, yielding "composite,
  provider, strips" and "memory, system, state". Removed -- it duplicates
  full-text search and crowds out real tags under the max_tags cap.
* The memory type was added as a tag despite type being a first-class field.
  Removed.

The taxonomy itself and the optional LLM suggestion are untouched.
---
--- a/src/hippocampai/pipeline/semantic_clustering.py
+++ b/src/hippocampai/pipeline/semantic_clustering.py
@@ -92,24 +92,27 @@
         """
         text_lower = memory.text.lower()
         suggested = set()
 
-        # Extract keywords (nouns, important words)
-        words = re.findall(r"\b[a-z]{4,}\b", text_lower)
-        word_counts = Counter(words)
-
-        # Add most common meaningful words
-        for word, count in word_counts.most_common(3):
-            if word not in {"that", "this", "with", "from", "have", "been", "were"}:
-                suggested.add(word)
-
-        # Add topic-based tags
+        # NOTE: the three most frequent 4+ letter words used to be added as tags
+        # here. On real memories that produced "composite, provider, strips" and
+        # "memory, system, state" -- no information a full-text search does not
+        # already have, and because the result is capped at max_tags it crowded
+        # out the tags that did mean something. Removed.
+
+        # Topic tags, matched on WORD BOUNDARIES.
+        # Previously this was `kw in text_lower`, a bare substring test, so:
+        #     "strips"  contains "trip"  -> travel
+        #     "rework"  contains "work"  -> work
+        #     "restore" contains "store" -> shopping
+        # which is why infrastructure notes came back tagged travel and shopping.
         for topic, keywords in self.topic_keywords.items():
-            if any(kw in text_lower for kw in keywords):
+            if any(re.search(r"\b" + re.escape(kw) + r"\b", text_lower) for kw in keywords):
                 suggested.add(topic)
 
-        # Add type-based tag
-        suggested.add(memory.type.value)
+        # The memory TYPE is deliberately NOT added as a tag: it is already a
+        # first-class field on the model, so tagging it duplicates data and
+        # spends one of the max_tags slots.
 
         # LLM-based tag suggestion if available
         if self.llm and len(suggested) < max_tags:
             llm_tags = self._llm_suggest_tags(memory.text)
